<title>UK: World natural rubber stocks fall in April - IRSG.</title>
<headline>World natural rubber stocks fall in April - IRSG.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-09-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>World stocks of natural rubber fell 90,000 tonnes in April 1996, far outweighing a 20,000 tonnes rise in synthetic rubber stocks, latest International Rubber Study Group (IRSG) data showed.</p>
<p>    Data in thousand tonnes  --  Apr'96     Mar'96     Apr'95</p>
<p>    Natural production		  410	  470	  420</p>
<p>    Natural consumption		 500	  510	  490</p>
<p>    Natural stocks		    1,560	1,650	1,610</p>
<p>    Synthetic production		810	  820	  810</p>
<p>    Synthetic consumption	     790	  820	  780</p>
<p>    Synthetic stocks		  2,040	2,020	1,930</p>
<p>London Newsrooom, +44 171 542 7771</p>
</text>
